<SoilDataTemplate>
  <SoilType href="Z:\Documents\Projects\Howleaky\Project data\HL projects\Greenwood\Soil\Greenwood Grey clay.soil" text="Greenwood 2026" Description="Greenwood Grey clay" Comments="Nov 2026 (24 Nov): layer 1 changed from 0-15 to 0-10 cm and layer 2 from 15-30 to 10-30 cm, the same top-layer configuration as the other site soils and the 0-10, 10-30 cm sampling increments. %vol limits unchanged; PAWC 258 -> 256 mm. Cona and CN not refitted.&#xA;Nov 2026 (16 Nov): RunoffCurveNumber is now the bare-soil CN at average wetness (CNReferenceWetness 0.25), converted on reading to the internal CN2 used by the uncapped AMC. Runoff unchanged.&#xA;Nov 2026 (15 Nov): kl removed; U set to 0; no-stress PAW fraction 0.75 in all vege files; Cona and CN2 refitted per site (runoff P:O = 1, minimum PAW RMSE), input-file mode from the revised vege files with no soil water resets; K rescaled for soil movement P:O = 1. Engine fix: days since wetting reset from the stage II total after rain (needed for U = 0).&#xA;Nov 2026: Watbal2026 joint three-site calibration (Greenmount, Greenwood, Wallumbilla) on cumulative P:O, run from revised vege files with no soil water resets. Shared: CN reduction at full cover 14.8, zero-till CN2 offset +5.4, SedCoverCoef 0.057, AMC howleaky, seasonal sediment factor off. Site: CN2, K, Cona, U, bottom drainage. See calibration/joint_2026 in the Southern Queensland small catchment data repository.&#xA;6 layer profile Based on measured soil water 1978 -1984&#xA;PAWC 240 mm&#xA;Measured using gravimetric soil cores to 150 cm depth in 0-10, 10,30, 30-60, 60-90,90-120, 120-150 cm increments&#xA;DMF 16/1/2012">
